  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "RBAC model (decisions 89, 109; ADR-0029)",
      "items": [
        "One screen per tab, gated actions — not two parallel UIs. \"Gated Actions\" above is that one screen: both roles land on it, sign-off controls just render only for Lead/Approver, since ADR-0029's whole checkpoint architecture assumes drafter and approver are different people",
        "Full tab order: Setup → Intake → Gap Analysis → Meeting → Findings → Approval → Audit Log — tabs unlock independently once their own data exists, not a hard phase-stepper (decision 83), since AG/pre-exit revision loops mean progress isn't strictly linear",
        "Settings/Admin (rubric editor, Notice Corpus Manager) and per-tab HITL detail live outside this diagram — see lfi-pipeline-v1.html and agent-specifications.md"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "How to read this diagram",
      "items": [
        "Role branches are edge-labeled, not decision diamonds — archify's workflow grammar has no gateway/fork-join primitive",
        "\"Auto-closes\" fires the instant preexit_status reaches proceeded_to_exit — a code-checkable terminal condition, same pattern as each agent's definition-of-done (ADR-0026)"
      ]
    }
  ]
